Z||000015||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||01:37 PM||||no im rite. the reason cleveland isnt in any fords now is it hasnt been made for years, except in Austrailia. The cleveland has lots more power potential than windsor. the cleveland heads are almost hemis. Youd get more power building up the 302 than youd ever get from the winsor. can you say Boss 302- not to mention 'little' 289 Cobra and GT40's. Smokey Yunick had a Ford to race in Nascar that ran the small block when everyone else was running 427/s. He was running away from everyone in practice at Daytona and due to politics Nascar disqualified his car before he actually raced it.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever2||12-31-2000||01:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Kind of want a late 60's fastback though.. Anyone have any experience with those? How are they speedwise?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I worked with a guy who collected 69 Mach I's, and all I know is... <I>FAST</I>!!!<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000017||JohnnyK||12-31-2000||03:10 PM||||And surely there are a lot of go-fast add on's for those 302's and 351's?||||reg||1
Z||000018||BBBAD GT||12-31-2000||03:29 PM||||roger:  The cleveland motor is a completely different motor from the windsor.  You are right about the heads, waaaay too big for the street.  The power potential is there, but only for over 5k rpms.  The aftermarket for the cleveland is almost zero compared to the 302/351 windsor, which can share heads and cam. The boss motors weren't the best street drivers with those big heads, and didn't do so well at the dragstrip (stock) compared to some modified 302/351's of today. <P>Go to any Ford shop, and ask them which motor they would build up, a windsor or a cleveland, and I bet 90% of them will say windsor.  <P>Johnny:  If you want a fast car, its going to cost money, period.  Remember, combo combo combo, just don't throw parts at whatever you are building and expect it to run like a bat outta hell without taking into consideration the whole combo.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||kong||12-31-2000||04:43 PM|||| If you want to go fast, there is a kit for a big block 429/460 swap into the newer stangs. But $ = speed, how fast do you want to go = how big is your bank account? If you're wanting to stay under 5k skip the stang and build up you fiero. If you're determined to build a stang. You can put cleveland heads on a 351W.Use 2v heads with a 4 bbl manifold though, the 4v breathes TOO well. You'll also have to drill a couple of holes in the block to open up the water jackets for the heads, But it is a fairly cheap way to get good hp gains for a 351W.||||reg||1
Z||000020||JohnnyK||12-31-2000||06:31 PM||||We are all talking about a later 60's 351 right? You can actually get mods for it? As for building up a Fiero, I don't know what your smoking, but it would cost a hell of a lot more to get a Fiero on par with Mustang performance.  I'd have to get a v8, v8 kit, suspension, and do something about that god awful clutch that I hate so much.||||reg||1
