Z||000023||JohnnyK||01-01-2001||02:53 AM||||I come here because I like the members here, and I trust their opinions. Sure, some will say "screw the 'stang, it is a Ford, and will never be fast and reliable", but I expect most have good answers regarding my questions. Geez, some people here ask questions totally off the wall, not even regarding cars!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000024||HF6582||01-02-2001||04:15 PM||||I have an 89 Mustang with the Ford Racing sportmans block in it. It is fuel injected and turns over 400hp at the crank, this a NA motor no nos or supercharging. It is the windsor variety. I can give you the run done on parts.<P>Use the windsor NOT the clevland!<P>The clevland had really one big favorable thing going for it, which is smaller main journals (able to turn more rpm).<P>The winsor is the only way to go on a street car.<P>You can do a carbed windsor cheap, fuel injection is a lot nicer.<P>Scott||||reg||1
