Z||000026||BBBAD GT||01-03-2001||02:16 PM||||Scott:<P>How about a run down of your 351 Stang (and $$), so JohnnyK can see what he's getting into.<P>I have the same sportsman shortblock, still in the crate in my garage, waiting for the 302 to split  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000027||HF6582||01-03-2001||06:47 PM||||Heres what I have off of the top of my head right now.<P>351 fox body oil pan <BR>351 intake FI or carb<BR>351 headers for fox body car<BR>351 dist.<BR>351 hamonic dampner and flywheel or flexplate<BR>acc. mounting bracket from ford racing (AC and PS or just PS)<BR>Cowl hood size depends on intake set up (mine is 4" with about 1" to spare)<BR>If 5 speed need tremec at min. Auto need C4 or AOD (AOD needs extensive mods for the torque output).<BR>302 motor mounts for a convertible or the new poly units that are out. <BR>Subframe connector are a must.<P>This is just a start of what I have in mine, sorry don't have prices right now.<P>Some items have a hefty price on them, so if you are serious do alot of research and ask lots of questions.<P>FI setup MUST upgrade fuel pump and line for reliabillity.<P>Its alot of work, but when its finished you will have a blast.<P>I'll look around and see what else I can dig up, this was all off of the top of my head.<P>Scott<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||JohnnyK||01-03-2001||09:39 PM||||I am planning on starting with a 429 Mach though?||||reg||1
Z||000029||BBBAD GT||01-04-2001||09:34 AM||||What Scott pointed out was the misc stuff needed to put a 351W in a fox body mustang, he didn't even get to what had to be done to the shortblock to get at his 400 flywheel HP figure (I'd assume heads/cam/intake/headers/exhaust/etc ... that adds up to over $2.5k in parts).  <P>429?  I guess money is no object then, because I doubt you'll find a decent running 429 early Mustang for cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000030||HF6582||01-04-2001||12:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BBBAD GT:<BR><B>What Scott pointed out was the misc stuff needed to put a 351W in a fox body mustang, he didn't even get to what had to be done to the shortblock to get at his 400 flywheel HP figure (I'd assume heads/cam/intake/headers/exhaust/etc ... that adds up to over $2.5k in parts).  <P>429?  I guess money is no object then, because I doubt you'll find a decent running 429 early Mustang for cheap.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What I posted was just to put the 351 in a fox body car.  As for the engine you have to determine what you what out of it in terms of HP and torgue.<P>To go the big block route, there are basically the same parts to fit it in the car.<P>You have to change the brake master cylinder to the smaller style (don't remember the years on that).<BR>Trans choices, most run a C6. Trans tunnel mods needed (BIG HAMMER USED HERE)to fit it in.<P>This is all for the fox bodied cars.<P>Scott<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000031||JohnnyK||01-04-2001||01:23 PM||||Well, I'm going to go searching today for a mach1 (Actually, I'm kind of hoping for a 351 variety), and when I find it, we will take it from there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Unless you guys think that the earlier (68's?) are better than the Mach1s.. I want a resto project (hopefully mostly aesthetic. I want to try painting, and I am really sick of doing mechanical.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000032||HF6582||01-04-2001||02:56 PM||||I wish I would known you were looking for an older Mustang. A '68 Mach 1 sold where I live cheap. <BR>Personally I like the old 289 Mustang, but '68 on you can put a big block in them.<P>Just look around, you'll find what you what.<P>Scott<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000033||FieroMaster88||01-05-2001||01:39 AM||||I know this makes me sound like a rice boy, but I am getting a Honda CRX this week for $100.  They sell these J-spec (japan spec) engine kits for pretty cheap.  I know a place for about $500 I can get a new Engine, Trans, wire harness and computer!  Probably a 1.6L Vtec.  If I do it right (no stickers, no big ass spoiler)  i can get the car into the 13's easy.  <P>For those of u worried about my sanity, I have plans for a Fiero with a quick ass 4 cyl.  Gonna do a HO Quad 4 with a Trubocharger and intercooled in a black coupe.   "Sniper Fiero"   Yes, I am really into 4 cyl engines.  see a lot of potential.  <P>Later<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1_1.jpg"> <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
